# =============================================================================
# R / RStudio project .gitignore
# Tailored for ecological analysis / R package work
# =============================================================================

# --- R workspace & history ----------------------------------------------------
# Prevent large .RData files and session history from entering Git
.RData
.RData.*
.Rhistory
.Rprofile
.Renviron

# RStudio project/user-specific files
.Rproj.user
.Rbuildignore
*.Rproj.user

# --- R package development ----------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts
*.tar.gz
*.Rcheck
*.Rinst
*.o
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib

# Documentation / manual builds
man/*.Rd
vignettes/*.pdf
README.Rmd
NEWS.Rmd

# Test & coverage
tests/testthat/_snaps
tests/testthat.Rout.fail
*.gcno
*.gcda
*.gcov

# --- Data & output -----------------------------------------------------------
# Large data / intermediate objects (adjust patterns to your project)
data-raw/*.csv
data-raw/*.rds
data-raw/*.RData
output/*.csv
output/*.rds
output/*.RData
output/*.pdf
output/*.png
output/*.Rmd

# Temporary R objects
*.rds
*.RDataTmp*
*.RData.bak
*.RData.old

# --- System / editor ---------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editor / IDE
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-*

# --- Logs & misc -------------------------------------------------------------
# R session logs
*.Rout
*.log

# renv / packrat (if used, uncomment as needed)
# renv/
# packrat/

# Quarto / R Markdown renders (keep source, ignore rendered)
*.html
*.docx
*.pptx
!README.md
!README.html

# --- Keep these (examples) ---------------------------------------------------
# Typically you DO want to track:
#   - R/             (package code)
#   - man/           (hand-edited .Rd if any)
#   - vignettes/*.Rmd
#   - tests/
#   - data/*.rda (small, curated datasets)
#   - DESCRIPTION, NAMESPACE, LICENSE, etc.